  "body": "Refs #683 (closed by #1009; this is the follow-up of its review, docs and comments only)\nClaim: cloud/i970-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/i970-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (cloud/review-1055-r2-opus)\n\n## Problem\nThe Opus review of #1009 (cloud/review-1009-opus, APPROVE on `f91f393`) left four non-blocking findings; the review of this PR found three more stale values.\n\n## Cause\n#1009 made `HTTPRequest.timeout` an idle limit for every request, but did not follow the callers and docs that still described a total limit or the old values, nor say what happens to images.\n\n## Change\n1. **Images** (Low): reader images (`ReaderImageFetcher`) and third-party image hosts (`ImageHostTable.request`) take `RequestTimeout.standard`, so they now follow the 10 s idle limit. Choice named in LOT-040: no legacy trace covers them (legacy loads images in the web view), so they get no value of their own; an image host that waits more than 10 s before its first byte now fails.\n2. **Wording** (Low): « idle limit » in `GiphyClient.swift:10`, `RehostClient.swift:12` (legacy `ReplyService.swift:1992` @ `2440d79` sets `timeoutInterval`, an idle limit, so the 60 s upload matches legacy) and `docs/lots/LOT-056-image-hosts.md:40`.\n3. **LOT-047:63** (Detail): « the 30 s page default » is 10 s.\n4. **Linux upload** (Detail): one comment on `dataWithIdleLimit`: only received bytes count there, so a request body that takes longer than the limit to send fails on Linux, which Apple's `timeoutInterval` does not do; the Linux build does not ship.\n5. **Round 1** (this PR's review): LOT-041 (global search « 15 s », topic search « 60 s ») and LOT-046:34 (« 15 s ») now give the #683 values. GAP-750 is not touched: its `gap-edit` is in the `### Ledger` of #1009, which the steward folds.\n\nNo code behaviour changes, no legacy behaviour changes (no `### Ledger`), no app file (no compile-check).\n\n## Tests\nNone added: comments and docs only. `swift build` and `swiftlint lint --strict` on `Packages/HFRKit/Sources` pass; `check-lot-deps.py` passes. Raised to the orchestrator, not changed here: `AQClient.timeout` is 20 s and cites `2440d79`, legacy at `2fe43da3` uses 10 s for AQ (`HFRNetworkTimeout.content`).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFtuGduNx3JqYjNFU4)_",
