   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, ad2e83504461bd555, head e4811cf93299a4359fcb3384f328d8e486e7413c): REQUEST CHANGES** — round 1, posted verbatim\n\n**Revue adversariale (Opus 5.5) : CHANGEMENTS DEMANDÉS** — tête e4811cf9\n\nThe four promised fixes are correct:\n- `ReaderImageFetcher.swift:50` and `ImageHostTable.swift:54` both take `RequestTimeout.standard`, which is 10.\n- The citation `ReplyService.swift:1992` @ 2440d79 really is `request.timeoutInterval = 60`. At 87fe0d1c the same line is `:2032`.\n- The new Linux comment in `URLSessionTransport.swift:108-109` describes `IdleWatchDelegate` correctly. Only `didReceive response` and `didReceive data` count as activity; there is no send callback.\n- The LOT-047 D4 row is right now.\n\nThe problems are elsewhere: three other documents still give timeout values from before #683.\n\n1. **Medium**, `docs/lots/LOT-041-endpoints.md:30-31`. Global search still says \"Timeout 15 s\" and topic search \"timeout 60 s\". The code says 10 s idle plus a 10 s total cap for global search, and 10 s for topic search (`HTTPRequest.swift:23-27`, `HFREndpoint+Search.swift:40-41,68`). Someone checking search against its spec would rebuild the old limits or call the code wrong (L08/L21). Fix: give the #683 values and link LOT-040.\n2. **Medium**, `docs/lots/LOT-046-search.md:34`. It says \"the global search timeout (15 s, LOT-041)\", which is the same stale value. Fix: \"10 s idle + 10 s total (LOT-040, #683)\".\n3. **Low**, `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md:100` (GAP-750). It says \"30 s (HFRNetwork `RequestTimeout.standard`)\", but that preset is 10 s now. The 30 s is `TopicReaderModel.waitLimit`, and that is how `TopicReaderModel.swift:116-119` puts it. Fix: since this is a ledger file, add a `gap-edit` to the PR's `### Ledger` section (for example `Swift: 30 s (TopicReaderModel.waitLimit)…`) rather than touching the file.\n\n**Checked:**\n- Read the diff against `origin/dev-swift`.\n- Grepped `Packages/HFRKit/Sources`, `App`, and `docs` for \"total\", \"15/30/60 s\" and `RequestTimeout`.\n- Read the legacy line at 2440d79 and at 87fe0d1c/2fe43da3.\n- Read the `IdleWatchDelegate` code.\n- Ran `swiftlint lint` on the three Swift files: clean.\n- I did not run `swift test`, since only comments changed in code.\n\n**Handled in `0b21f55` (one commit):**\n1. LOT-041: global search « 10 s idle plus a 10 s cap on the whole transfer », topic search « 10 s idle », both linking LOT-040.\n2. LOT-046: « 10 s idle + 10 s total, LOT-040, #683 ».\n3. Not repeated here: the same `gap-edit` of GAP-750 (« 30 s (the reader's own wait limit, independent of the 10 s request idle limit since #683) ») is already in the `### Ledger` section of #1009, which merged; the steward folds it into the file, and a second edit of the same cell would duplicate it. The ledger file is not touched by this PR.\n\nClass check beyond the finding: no other source or doc still says « total » for a timeout; `AQClient.timeout` (20 s, cites `2440d79`; legacy at `2fe43da3` uses `HFRNetworkTimeout.content` = 10 s for AQ per #683's issue text) is a parity question, not wording, so it is left alone and raised to the orchestrator.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
